cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Claude-SpinDynamics, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Claude-SpinDynamics: a GPU-accelerated, dual-precision micromagnetic simulator"
abstract: >-
  Claude-SpinDynamics (Claude-SD) is a C++20/CUDA micromagnetic simulator with a
  Python API that solves the Landau-Lifshitz-Gilbert (and stochastic LLG)
  equation on structured grids. It offers both single and double precision,
  cuFFT and VkFFT demag backends, native spin-orbit/spin-transfer torques, DMI,
  RKKY, magnetoelastic and surface anisotropy, per-cell materials, and adaptive
  integrators, validated against the muMAG standard problems and cross-checked
  against mumax3, mumax+ and MuMax-CO.
type: software
